## Hands-on Drills

### Drill 1: Manifest Creation and Scaling

1. **Declarative Manifest Deployment**:

   ```bash
   cd 01-basic-deployment
   kubectl apply -f web-frontend-deployment.yaml
   kubectl get deployment cka-lab-web-frontend -o wide
   kubectl get pods -l app.kubernetes.io/name=cka-lab-web-frontend
   ```

2. **Imperative Generation with Dry-Run**:

   Rapidly generate a production-ready manifest without creating the resource:

   ```bash
   kubectl create deployment cka-lab-cache-service \
     --image=redis:7-alpine \
     --replicas=2 \
     --port=6379 \
     --dry-run=client -o yaml > cache-service.yaml
   ```

3. **Imperative Scaling**:

   ```bash
   kubectl scale deployment cka-lab-web-frontend --replicas=5
   kubectl rollout status deployment/cka-lab-web-frontend
   ```

